# Docs and plans

- Three kinds, three readers: reader docs (`services/<name>/docs/*.mdx`, `apps/<name>/docs/*.mdx`)
  for people using a service; guides (`docs/guides/`) for people changing it; ADRs (`docs/adr/`)
  for decisions. Update whichever the change affects, in the same commit.
- Reader docs describe what the code does today. A limit the spec mentions but nothing enforces is
  written as "not enforced yet", never as a feature.
- Link pages by file (`./errors.mdx`, `../openapi.yaml#operationId`) so the docs check can follow
  them. A `service` section has a quickstart; mirror `services/comms-email/docs` for the rest.
- ADRs: a new number for a new decision; supersede, don't rewrite, an accepted one. Fix a mistaken
  detail in an ADR only on the unmerged branch that introduced it. Keep `docs/adr/README.md` in
  number order.
- Plans: tick a slice only when every part of it works; write what's left under an unticked one.
  Update the step's status in the plan and in `docs/plans/README.md`.
- LAUNCH.md is the runbook agents follow exactly: a new service, port, env var or database goes
  there, with a check, and with how to update an existing machine.
- Changelog: one bullet per commit under today's date, plain words, linking the doc.
